<!--
  MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1 Wave C — FeralGrazer creature port.
  Ported from mlie.starwarsanimalcollection's `FeralGrazer` ThingDef/
  PawnKindDef pair (Races_Animal_SW.xml, workshop folder 3497316713),
  renamed under the RSW_ tier prefix. Geometry/stats/comps copied verbatim.
  Body: the donor's `body` is the vanilla Core
  `QuadrupedAnimalWithHoovesAndHorn` — no BodyDef port needed.

  `leatherDef`/`specificMeatDef` both needed new resources this pass —
  `RSW_Leather_Nerf`/`RSW_Nerf_Meat` (RSW_MlieWaveC_Resources.xml). The
  donor's Leather_Nerf shares the exact same texPath as the already-ported
  RSW_Leather_Tough (swresource/Leather_Tough) — reused, no new leather art
  extracted. Meat_Nerf (swresource/Meat_Nerf) newly extracted this pass.

  `canCrossBreedWith` (Grazer, FeralNerf, Nerf) originally left pointing at
  the donor's still-bare, still-unported defNames — first port to carry
  this field. **Updated Pass 8 (2026-09-17)**: FeralNerf and Nerf are now
  ported (RSW_FeralNerf.xml/RSW_Nerf.xml) — renamed to RSW_FeralNerf/
  RSW_Nerf below. `Grazer` stays bare: it is not in this item's Wave C
  worklist (its donor ThingDef exists but has no row in
  cast_assignment.csv, out of scope), and Mlie stays active so the
  cross-reference remains functionally correct.

  Sounds repoint to the already-absorbed sound wave
  (RSW_Pawn_FeralGrazer_*, 2026-09-02). texPaths are unchanged text —
  extracted art sits at Textures/swanimals/FeralGrazer/ (extract_bundle.py
  against the same AssetBundle every prior wave used).

  Wired into the live cast this same pass: Desert (0.1) — per
  cast_assignment.csv's current row for this species, repointed from the
  bare "FeralGrazer" entry in cast_assignment.csv / BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml.
  No `*ArtOverride` mod exists for this species (checked before porting).
-->
<Defs>
<ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase" ADogSaidBody="LegsTail">
    <defName>RSW_FeralGrazer</defName>
    <label>feral grazer</label>
    <description>These slow-moving herbivorous mammalia were native to Alderaan. 'Feral' or 'wild' grazers were significantly leaner than the fatter and more well-fed domestic grazer; however both species were distantly related to Nerfs. Their horns, tough leathery hides and fat layers acted as an additional defense against predation.</description>
